                                          ] ;
                          :name_en "Shoulder and arm training"@en ;
                          mao:ontoMA_name_zh "肩臂训练"@zh-cn ;
                          mao:ontoMA_otherName_zh "肩膊訓練"@zh-hk ;
                          rdfs:comment "Conditioning exercises targeting the shoulder joints and arms; a sub-type of physical training common in martial arts warm-up and conditioning regimens."@en ;
                          rdfs:label "Shoulder_arm_training"@en .


###  http://EncodingActs.github.io/annotated/MAon/spar_training
mao:spar_training rdf:type owl:Class ;
                  rdfs:subClassOf mao:training_method ,
                                  [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                    owl:onProperty mao:type_of ;
                                    owl:someValuesFrom mao:training_method
                                  ] ;
                  :name_en "Sparring"@en ;
                  mao:ontoMA_name_zh "對練"@zh-hk ;
                  mao:ontoMA_otherName_zh "對拆"@zh-hk ;
                  rdfs:comment "Sparring is a form of training common to many combat sports and is considered the closest thing to a real fight without actually fighting. Usually, two persons are involved in sparring training, yet more is possible."@en ;
                  rdfs:label "Sparring"@en .


###  http://EncodingActs.github.io/annotated/MAon/stance
mao:stance rdf:type owl:Class ;
           rdfs:subClassOf mao:footwork ,
                           [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                             owl:onProperty mao:type_of ;
                             owl:someValuesFrom mao:footwork
                           ] ;
           :name_en "Stance"@en ;
           :name_romanCAN "Maa Bou"@en ;
           :name_romanMAN "Ma bu"@en ;
           mao:ontoMA_name_zh "馬步"@zh ;
           rdfs:comment "In martial arts, stances are the distribution, foot orientation and body positions (particularly the legs and torso) adopted when attacking, defending, advancing, or retreating."@en ;
           rdfs:label "Stance" .


###  http://EncodingActs.github.io/annotated/MAon/sweeping_tech
mao:sweeping_tech rdf:type owl:Class ;
                  rdfs:subClassOf mao:leg_tech ,
                                  [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                    owl:onProperty mao:type_of ;
                                    owl:someValuesFrom mao:leg_tech
                                  ] ;
                  :name_en "Sweeping technique"@en ;
                  mao:ontoMA_name_zh "掃腿"@zh-hk ;
                  rdfs:comment "Sweeping leg techniques involve a lateral or circular low leg movement intended to destabilise or unbalance an opponent."@en ;
                  rdfs:label "Sweeping_tech"@en .


###  http://EncodingActs.github.io/annotated/MAon/symbolic_animal
mao:symbolic_animal rdf:type owl:Class ;
                    rdfs:subClassOf mao:E77_persistent_item ,
                                    [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                      owl:onProperty mao:type_of ;
                                      owl:someValuesFrom mao:E77_persistent_item
                                    ] ;
                    :name_en "Symbolic Animal"@en ;
                    mao:ontoMA_name_zh "象徵動物"@zh-hk ;
                    rdfs:comment "Certain martial arts styles may associate themselves with one or multiple creatures or living things as symbols, indicated by the property has_symbol pointing to an instance of Symbolic_animal. It is widely held that many martial arts styles draw inspiration from the habits and moves of specific creatures like animals in designing their movement and tactical patterns. For example, the various Praying Mantis styles are inspired by the mantis (insect), and the White Crane kung fu imitates the crane (bird)."@en ;
                    rdfs:label "Symbolic_animal"@en .


###  http://EncodingActs.github.io/annotated/MAon/training_method
mao:training_method rdf:type owl:Class ;
                    rdfs:subClassOf owl:Thing ,
                                    [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                      owl:onProperty mao:trains ;
                                      owl:someValuesFrom mao:MA_technique
                                    ] ,
                                    [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                      owl:onProperty mao:uses ;
                                      owl:someValuesFrom mao:armament
                                    ] ,
                                    [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                      owl:onProperty mao:uses ;
                                      owl:someValuesFrom mao:training_tool
                                    ] ;
                    :name_en "Training method"@en ;
                    mao:ontoMA_name_zh "訓練方法"@zh-hk ;
                    rdfs:comment "The class Training_method encompasses methods created or adapted by a teaching master for learners to practice specific techniques while developing necessary physical qualities and comprehending the movement principles embedded. Instances of this class may feature a unitary exercise - a Form, or a series of exercises constituting a set - an instance of Form_set. While forms and form sets can vary significantly across styles and systems, they all serve training purposes. Another two categories of training methods crucial for developing martial arts skills are Physical_training and Sparring, both not codified. In any of these situations, the trains property is established to connect an instance of Training_method to one or more of Technique if the former contributes to the development of the latter."@en ;
                    rdfs:label "Training_method"@en .


###  http://EncodingActs.github.io/annotated/MAon/training_tool
mao:training_tool rdf:type owl:Class ;
                  rdfs:subClassOf mao:E22_man_made_obj ,
                                  [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                    owl:onProperty mao:simulates ;
                                    owl:someValuesFrom mao:armament
                                  ] ,
                                  [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                    owl:onProperty mao:type_of ;
                                    owl:someValuesFrom mao:E22_man_made_obj
                                  ] ;
                  :name_en "Training Tool"@en ;
                  mao:ontoMA_name_zh "訓練工具"@zh-hk ;
                  rdfs:comment "Training tools refer to objects created to simulate a weapon - an entity of armament, or part of it, to train a specific technique or physical qualities. The property simulates is utilized to indicate a possible analogy."@en ;
                  rdfs:label "Training_tool"@en .


###  http://EncodingActs.github.io/annotated/MAon/waist_training
mao:waist_training rdf:type owl:Class ;
                   rdfs:subClassOf mao:physical_training ,
                                   [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                     owl:onProperty mao:type_of ;
                                     owl:someValuesFrom mao:physical_training
                                   ] ;
                   :name_en "Waist training"@en ;
                   mao:ontoMA_name_zh "腰部訓練"@zh-hk ;
                   rdfs:comment "Conditioning exercises targeting the waist and core; critical in Chinese martial arts for developing rotational power (发腰)."@en ;
                   rdfs:label "Waist_training"@en .


###  http://EncodingActs.github.io/annotated/MAon/weapon_tech
